# Design system conventions

## Tokens, never hardcoded values
- Colors come from `styles/tokens.css` custom properties (`--background-primary`, `--foreground-secondary`, `--border-primary`, ...). Both themes must work — check `:root[data-theme="dark"]` derivations before adding a raw hex.
- Radii/spacing/typography: `--radius-*`, `--space-*`, `--font-ui`, `--font-brand`.
- Needing a "slightly different" color? Prefer `color-mix(in srgb, var(--token) N%, var(--other-token))` over new hex values.

## Components
- Reuse the UI kit first: `Button`, `IconButton`, `Badge`, `Modal`, `Field`/`Input`/`TextArea`/`Select`, `Icon`, `Tile`, `Menu` from `components/ui`.
- `Field` renders a `<div>`, not `<label>` — label activation double-fires hidden inputs. Don't "fix" it back.
- Icons: only names from the harvested set (`components/ui/Icon.tsx`, SVGs normalized to `currentColor`). New icons come from Figma, normalized the same way.
- Dialogs/dropdowns must close on Escape (`useEscapeKey`) and outside click.
- Citation/source links never use `<a href>` — route through `window.api.openExternal` (main validates https).

## CSS placement
- Workspace chrome + surfaces: `styles/workspace.css`. UI kit: `styles/ui.css`. Home + toasts + legacy: `styles.css`. Delete dead CSS when retiring a component.

## Store & interaction
- Document mutations go through the store's `save*` actions (`savePortfolio`, `saveIps`, `saveWatchlist`, `saveAlerts`) — optimistic local update + validated persist + error notice on failure.
- Long-running scripts run through `lib/jobs.ts` `runJob` (job state, PHASE/PROGRESS mirroring, reload on success). Don't hand-roll job wiring per button.
- App-wide shortcuts live in `App.tsx` — never inside a component that unmounts. Always guard: skip when typing in INPUT/TEXTAREA/SELECT/contentEditable.
- Long lists: cap visible rows and scroll within (`clip-list-capped` pattern).

## Voice
- Honesty is part of the design language: no advice framing, no hype, disclaimers on generated research surfaces, and "dropped claims" counts stay visible.
